<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leuthari</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 554</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Leutharis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leuthari was an Alemannic duke who, with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/butilin">Butilin</a>, led a Frankish and Alemannic army into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 553 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gothic-war-535-554">Gothic War</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrogoths">Ostrogoths</a>. After raiding southern Italy he turned north with his plunder, but his army was ravaged by disease in northern Italy, and Leuthari himself died of it in 554 before reaching home.</p></div>
